## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical DP with fixed-length window constraints and reconstruction, mirroring analytics batching scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes with exact segment count
- Prefix sums for fast interval sums
- Reconstruction path tracking

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarraysWithBounds(A, k, L, R){
  const n = A.length;
  const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const neg = -1/0; const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(neg));
  for(let i=0;i<=n;i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  const take = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      for(let len=L; len<=R && len<=i; len++){
        if (dp[i-len][t-1] !== neg) {
          const val = dp[i-len][t-1] + (P[i]-P[i-len]);
          if (val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = len; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return {maxSum: dp[n][k], take}
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to model non-crossing, higher-arity structures with DP and reconstruct a solution.

## Key Concepts

- DP state dp[i][t] for i and t
- Non-crossing triple formation
- Reconstruction via backpointers
- Time/space trade-offs and optimization path

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxTriples(A, n, k) {
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prv = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      if (t>0) {
        for (let i1=1; i1<i; i1++) {
          for (let j=i1+1; j<i; j++) {
            const prev = (i1>=2 ? dp[i1-1][t-1] : (t-1===0 ? 0 : -Infinity));
            const val = prev + A[i1-1]*A[j-1]*A[i-1];
            if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; prv[i][t] = {i1, j}; }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction logic would backtrack using prv
  return {value: dp[n][k], triples: []};
}
```

